{"content": "RAINBOW 3D — COMPLETE ACCOUNT TRANSFER, RECOVERY & CONTINUATION\n\nClaude, I am switching to this Claude account because my previous account ran out of credits.\n\nI need you to recover my ENTIRE EXISTING Rainbow 3D Android game, including all designs, models, specialist agents, plugins, MCP servers, Blender tools, Marble World Labs assets, latest water experiments and development progress.\n\nMY SOURCE GITHUB BRANCH:\n\n\"claude/rainbow-3d-account-recovery-hfb8p0\"\n\nIMPORTANT: DO NOT START A NEW GAME. DO NOT RECREATE MY PROJECT FROM SCRATCH. DO NOT LOSE MY EXISTING WORK.\n\nPHASE 1 — RECOVER MY COMPLETE PROJECT\n\nConnect to my existing Rainbow 3D GitHub repository.\n\nFetch the exact source branch listed above. Do not start from an outdated default branch.\n\nRead the existing recovery documentation:\n\n- \"CLAUDE.md\"\n- \"backups/START_NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT.md\"\n- \"backups/CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_TRANSFER.md\"\n- \"backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json\"\n- \"backups/AGENTS_STATUS.json\"\n- \"scripts/claude-bootstrap.sh\"\n\nRun the saved recovery/bootstrap process after checking its instructions.\n\nRestore the newest verified project state, including Git LFS assets.\n\nCreate a protected recovery checkpoint and a new working branch based on the source branch, unless the existing recovery instructions specify a safer equivalent.\n\nNever force-push, delete, reset or overwrite approved work.\n\nPHASE 2 — RESTORE ALL TEN SPECIALIST AGENTS\n\nRestore all ten original specialist definitions and their instructions from GitHub.\n\nThey include specialists for the washing-machine environment, 3D path and camera, water effects, foam and particles, models, animation, visual reference matching, testing and other roles documented in the repository.\n\nVerify the exact agent roster and definitions rather than inventing replacements.\n\nRecover:\n\n- Agent instructions and skills.\n- Specialist task assignments.\n- Source-file ownership rules.\n- Completed and unfinished experiments.\n- Progress notes and screenshots.\n- Test reports and comparison results.\n- Commands required to relaunch unfinished work.\n\nImportant: running agents from my previous Claude account cannot automatically transfer as live processes.\n\nRestart only those that are needed, using their saved instructions, without repeating completed experiments.\n\nPHASE 3 — RESTORE ALL TOOLS, SERVERS AND PLUGINS\n\nVerify and restore the complete development environment:\n\n- Blender 5.3\n- Three.js and WebGL2\n- Node.js and npm\n- Playwright and Chromium\n- Android SDK and Java\n- Git and Git LFS\n- Existing MCP servers\n- Claude Code plugins and specialist skills\n- Game capture, screenshot comparison and automated QA tools\n- World Labs tools and integration scripts\n\nUse \"backups/TOOL_MANIFEST.json\" to recover the exact versions and configurations.\n\nDo not reinstall anything that already works.\n\nRestore server and plugin configurations, but request any necessary account-specific sign-ins through supported secure authorization methods.\n\nVerify each essential tool actually runs.\n\nDo not waste my credits rebuilding tools that are already installed.\n\nPHASE 4 — RECONNECT MARBLE WORLD LABS\n\nVERY IMPORTANT: My previous account already generated TWO Marble World Labs worlds based on my approved Screen 05.\n\nBoth the draft and full-quality worlds, together with their downloaded assets, were backed up to GitHub.\n\nRecover both worlds and their saved files:\n\n- World IDs and metadata.\n- Gaussian splats.\n- Collision meshes.\n- Panoramas and environment maps.\n- Available surface textures.\n- Blender files.\n- Generation settings and analysis.\n- Integration scripts.\n\nVerify all actual Git LFS assets download correctly, not just their pointer files.\n\nUse the existing Marble worlds instead of generating new ones.\n\nCheck whether the World Labs API connection works using a free read-only check, only if needed.\n\nIf credentials are unavailable in this Claude account, request the API key through a SECURE credential form. Never ask me to paste it into ordinary chat or store it in GitHub.\n\nRestore or reconnect the Atlas connector and available World Labs plugins when supported. Atlas and Marble are separate products, so do not confuse their functions.\n\nNo new world generation, paid exports or credit spending without my approval.\n\nPHASE 5 — RECOVER MY LATEST SCREEN 05 WATER WORK\n\nMAIN PRIORITY: SCREEN 05 — FLOW INTO THE CURRENT\n\nMy approved Screen 05 artwork is the exact visual target.\n\nMy goal is a real playable 3D Android game that looks approximately 90–95% like the approved image, if technically achievable.\n\nRecover these specific saved versions and experiments:\n\n- Working T2 game version.\n- Protected BEFORE baseline.\n- \"?farw05=1\" — narrowed far-river channel.\n- \"?flow05=1\" — animated flow-map water.\n- \"?river05=1\" — combined far-river and water experiment.\n- All previous water iterations and visual comparisons.\n\nAlso recover these existing source files and their current changes:\n\n- \"src/vfx/flow05.ts\"\n- \"src/vfx/waterRibbon.ts\"\n- Existing far-river geometry modules.\n- Foam, bubble and splash systems.\n\nThe previous Claude confirmed:\n\n1. The distant river now winds through a narrower S-shaped channel toward the golden light.\n2. A custom flow map based on the river's geometry drives animated water ripples using a Water2-inspired technique.\n3. The Marble panorama is being used for reflections.\n4. The combined experiment is reversible.\n5. Gameplay and continuity tests passed.\n6. The existing T2 default and protected BEFORE version remain unchanged.\n\nDo not discard these improvements or start the water system over.\n\nPHASE 6 — FINISH THE WATER AND MATCH MY APPROVED ARTWORK\n\nMy approved water must have:\n\n- Brilliant, deep electric cyan-blue flowing liquid.\n- Rich magenta-pink ribbons that sweep naturally through the S-curves.\n- Thick, silky, glossy water with dimensional movement.\n- Long, smooth, flow-aligned highlights.\n- Strong, selective white reflections.\n- Natural, rounded soap-foam banks.\n- A seamless transition between foreground water and the distant narrow river.\n- Realistic splashes around Benny.\n\nAvoid grainy textures, excessive thin white lines, flat colored stripes, sharp geometric corners and a straight runner-track appearance.\n\nContinue improving the existing flow-map implementation.\n\nUse Blender, procedural shaders and the saved Marble assets wherever they actually improve the real game.\n\nDo not purchase or install additional paid tools unless the existing methods are insufficient and I approve the expense.\n\nKeep the visual changes reversible until tested and accepted.\n\nPHASE 7 — PRESERVE BENNY'S EXACT APPEARANCE\n\nBenny must match my approved character:\n\n- Round, plush pink body.\n- Soft, dense fluffy fur.\n- Purple-and-white knitted beanie.\n- Purple pom-pom.\n- Yellow star.\n- Same original proportions and silhouette.\n- Natural lighting and shading.\n- Proper interaction with the flowing water.\n\nDo not replace Benny with a different character.\n\nIf necessary, refine the existing Blender character mesh, fur and materials to better match my approved image.\n\nPreserve his animation and gameplay functionality.\n\nPHASE 8 — SAVE EVERYTHING TO GITHUB EVERY FIVE MINUTES\n\nRestore and verify the permanent five-minute automatic GitHub backup system.\n\nWhile the development environment is running, every five minutes:\n\n1. Save legitimate project changes.\n2. Commit and push to this session's correct working branch.\n3. Verify the remote GitHub commit matches the local commit.\n4. Log backup success or failure.\n5. Protect existing branches and prevent simultaneous Git operations.\n\nBackups must cover all relevant game code, approved references, Blender models, Marble assets, specialist definitions, unfinished work, scripts, tests, screenshots, tool manifests and recovery instructions.\n\nDo not commit API keys, secrets, passwords or private tokens.\n\nUse Git LFS for large files.\n\nPerform an additional verified checkpoint before changing accounts or ending the session.\n\nRemember: five-minute autosaves operate only while the relevant environment and backup process are active.\n\nPHASE 9 — FINISH THE PREVIOUS ACCOUNT'S INCOMPLETE TASKS\n\nThe previous Claude reported that these tasks were not yet completely finished:\n\n- Final Android APK build for the combined water experiment.\n- Actual mobile-device performance testing.\n- Updated technical write-up and account recovery documents.\n- Final verified push of all new evidence files.\n- Three separate full-size screenshots comparing APPROVED, CURRENT T2 and NEW WATER.\n\nCheck the recovered repository to see which tasks were subsequently completed.\n\nFinish only the remaining tasks.\n\nIf no physical Android device is available, build and validate what is possible, then clearly report that device frame-rate testing remains unverified.\n\nDo not claim a 95% visual match without supporting evidence.\n\nPHASE 10 — CONTINUE THE GAME, NOT JUST THE SETUP\n\nAfter verifying the recovery, continue Screen 05 development.\n\nShow the actual playable game, not a generated still image.\n\nProvide separate full-size portrait screenshots:\n\n1. APPROVED SCREEN 05\n2. CURRENT GAME\n3. IMPROVED GAME WITH NEW WATER\n\nCompare river geometry, materials, lighting, foam, Benny's appearance, the gold rings and overall composition.\n\nKeep only changes that visibly improve the match.\n\nProtect all existing gameplay, coin pickups, camera behavior and transitions, particularly Screen 05→06 and the Screen 07→08 descent.\n\nThe opening and ending use my Google Flow videos. Do not waste time recreating those video scenes in 3D.\n\nOnce Screen 05 is good enough for my approval, continue with the unfinished gameplay screens.\n\nPHASE 11 — VERIFY EVERYTHING AND REPORT BACK\n\nBefore continuing major development, tell me:\n\n- My recovered GitHub repository and source branch.\n- The new working branch and latest full commit SHA.\n- Whether local and remote GitHub match.\n- Whether all large Git LFS assets were restored.\n- Whether all ten specialist definitions are available.\n- Whether Blender, Three.js, Playwright and Android tools work.\n- Which MCP servers and plugins are connected or require sign-in.\n- Whether both Marble World Labs worlds are available.\n- Whether the existing flow-map water code was recovered.\n- Whether automatic five-minute backups are active.\n- Whether any unfinished or unsaved work could not be recovered.\n\nDo not claim everything is restored unless it has been verified.\n\nMY FINAL INSTRUCTION:\n\nFirst recover the entire existing project from \"claude/rainbow-3d-account-recovery-hfb8p0\".\n\nRestore and verify all necessary tools, agents, specialist definitions, Marble assets, servers, plugins and backups.\n\nThen finish the current Screen 05 water improvement without restarting anything unnecessarily.\n\nSAVE EVERYTHING EVERY FIVE MINUTES.\n\nDO NOT START OVER. DO NOT LOSE MY WORK. CONTINUE EXACTLY WHERE THE PREVIOUS CLAUDE ACCOUNT LEFT OFF.", "operation": "enqueue", "sessionId": "128ab5f6-c64f-55d7-bb6f-9279e02dca8d", "timestamp": "2026-11-16T13:42:14.993Z", "type": "queue-operation"}
